  "system": {
    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Galaxy_at_War\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy at War\">Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy at War</a></i> </p><p>The DC-17m Interchangeable Weapon System (also called the DC-17m ICWS) is a weapon unique to <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Clone_Commandos\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Clone Commandos\">Clone Commandos</a>. The varying demands of the battlefield and the Clone Commandos' atypical missions led BlasTech to design this weapon to fill three different roles. </p><p>The basic configuration is a standard <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Blaster_Rifle\" title=\"Blaster Rifle\">Blaster Rifle</a>. Additional attachments, however, can be added to transform the weapon into a Sniper Rifle or an Anti-Armor Grenade Launcher. <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Clone_Commandos\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Clone Commandos\">Clone Commandos</a> appreciate the versatility of the ICWS, which reduces the weight they carry by reducing the number of their weapons. </p><p>An Interchangeable Rifle System can be switched among three different modes: standard Blaster-Rifle mode, Sniper-Rifle mode, and Anti-Armor mode. Switching Weapon modes is a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Standard_Action\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Standard Action\">Standard Action</a>. </p><h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Blaster-Rifle_Mode\">Blaster-Rifle Mode</span></h3><p>In Blaster-Rifle mode, the ICWS functions like a regular <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Blaster_Rifle\" title=\"Blaster Rifle\">Blaster Rifle</a>. </p><h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Sniper-Rifle_Mode\">Sniper-Rifle Mode</span></h3><p>When the ICWS is changed to Sniper-Rifle mode, the weapon includes a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Targeting_Scope\" title=\"Targeting Scope\">Targeting Scope</a> (Standard), so there is no penalty to attack at Short <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Range\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Range\">Range</a>. However, the wielder takes a -2 penalty against targets at unmodified Point-Blank <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Range\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Range\">Range</a>. </p><p><b>Accurate:</b> This weapon mode takes no penalty when firing at targets at Short&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Range\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Range\">Range</a>. </p><h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Anti-Armor_Mode\">Anti-Armor Mode</span></h3><p>When the ICWS is in Anti-Armor mode, the Weapon functions as a single-shot <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Grenade_Launcher\" title=\"Grenade Launcher\">Grenade Launcher</a> that fires special Anti-Armor Rounds (3-Square <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Burst\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Burst\">Burst</a> radius), each weighing 1 kg and costing 400 credits. In this mode, the ICWS is considered a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Heavy_Weapon\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Heavy Weapon\">Heavy Weapon</a>. </p><p><b>Special:</b>&nbsp;This is an&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Area_Attack\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Area Attack\">Area Attack</a>&nbsp;Weapon. </p>",
